base.joinpath('16_OPERATOR_GATE_CHECKLIST.md').write_text('''# CAE Operator Gate Checklist\n\nUse this after each mandate. Do not review only whether files exist. Review whether the claimed architectural property was actually established.\n\n## 1. Scope\n- [ ] The agent touched only authorized files and systems.\n- [ ] Adjacent problems were recorded rather than opportunistically fixed.\n- [ ] The output matches the mandate objective.\n\n## 2. Authority\n- [ ] Definition authority is explicit.\n- [ ] Runtime authority is explicit.\n- [ ] Change/promotion authority is explicit.\n- [ ] No source/projection mismatch was silently ignored.\n\n## 3. Evidence\n- [ ] Every major claim has an evidence class.\n- [ ] Runtime claims were tested against the real environment where relevant.\n- [ ] A test result is not being treated as wider proof than it supports.\n\n## 4. Taste / reward-hacking\n- [ ] At least one false-proof case was attempted.\n- [ ] The test could not pass by satisfying only superficial structure.\n- [ ] For editorial work, I inspected at least one positive and one hard-negative example.\n- [ ] Score inflation, duplicate-source inflation, and generic-output paths were considered where relevant.\n\n## 5. Lineage\n- [ ] IDs and versions remain traceable.\n- [ ] Evidence can be traced back to source/media.\n- [ ] Derived artifacts can be recomputed or their derivation is recorded.\n\n## 6. State / isolation\n- [ ] Workspace/Guest scope is preserved where applicable.\n- [ ] Historical state was not destructively overwritten.\n- [ ] Receipts/events exist for authoritative state changes.\n\n## 7. Stop discipline\n- [ ] The agent asked the exact gate question.\n- [ ] The next mandate has not started early.\n\n## Operator decision record\n\n```text\nMandate:\nDecision: APPROVE / REJECT / RETURN FOR REPAIR / DEFER\nEvidence reviewed:\nFalse-proof cases reviewed:\nTaste review:\nKnown limitations:\nAuthorized next mandate:\nOperator:\nTimestamp:\n```\n''', encoding='utf-8')

